[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: VeloSim toolchain and standalone schematic requirements

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Trace: global.json, Directory.Build.props, Makefile and tools/VeloSim.Build
implement the toolchain selection and framework paths. apps/SchematicLab keeps
the imported component/source and command requirements. WebHost/StartupCommand.cs
and StartupOptions.cs implement finite CLI outcomes; WebHost/Program.cs enforces
localhost and source-generated failure JSON. Solver/SolverLocation.cs supplies
installed-relative lookup for WebHost and Mcp/Program.cs. Tests/StandaloneStartupTests.cs
checks boundary, deployment, malformed-input and seeded properties. scripts/Publish-Schematic.ps1,
Launch-Schematic.ps1 and Test-SchematicBundle.ps1 create/run/verify distributions;
Tests/Bundle.Tests.ps1 checks refusal boundaries. scripts/Test-Schematic.ps1
checks actual TRX outcomes. docs/csharp-modernization.md records language choices
and verification limitations; docs/schematic-import-evidence.json records import
integrity and the original baseline. Draft status does not imply general HDL,
analog or model-family qualification.
Book interaction trace: Core/InteractionPolicy.cs and LessonSession.cs enforce
typed lock/read commands and parameter-only history; CircuitBridge.cs and
BridgeDraft.cs enforce unchanged F/H connections at the asynchronous analysis
boundary. Web/Program.cs and WebHost/Program.cs provide required deployment
bootstrap; Mcp/Program.cs and LessonTools.cs reuse the same policy/commands.
Tests/InteractionPolicyTests.cs, Tests/BookBrowserSmoke.cjs and scripts/McpSmoke.cs
verify the bounded contracts. docs/live-lessons.md and examples/wally-live-rc.qmd
describe deployment/readiness; actual WALLY rendering and shared visible-session
agent control remain open. See docs/schematic-book-verification.md for current
counts, coverage scope, seeds, package provenance and unresolved checks.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-TOOLCHAIN-NET11-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Released .NET 11 toolchain
STATEMENT: >>>
Maintained VeloSim C# projects and included schematic projects shall build with
released SDK 11.0.100 and target net11.0. SDK selection, framework-dependent
paths, package locks, examples and build instructions shall agree. Verification
shall distinguish successful compilation, runtime execution and unavailable
native/platform coverage. The RC SDK shall not be required by this repository.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-SCHEMATIC-OWNERSHIP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Versioned schematic subproject
STATEMENT: >>>
The complete schematic source, requirements, tests, UI, solver adapter and MCP
host shall reside under apps/SchematicLab in VeloSim. Import shall retain its
history and stable requirements/command identifiers. Existing checkout data
shall not be discarded. Core shall remain independent of UI and HDL engines.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-SCHEMATIC-STANDALONE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Relocatable standalone web application
STATEMENT: >>>
A standalone schematic distribution shall contain its server and published
browser assets, and shall run outside the source checkout without building
the HDL simulator. Its default assets shall resolve relative to the installed
application, independent of current working directory. Packaging shall record
file hashes, runtime requirements and any included external solver provenance.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-SCHEMATIC-STARTUP-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Typed bounded startup commands
STATEMENT: >>>
Startup shall parse bounded explicit arguments into serve, help or error
commands. Duplicate or unknown options, missing values, invalid numeric ports
and invalid explicit paths shall fail before starting a server. Help shall
not require assets or a solver and shall not open interactive dialogs.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-SCHEMATIC-LOOPBACK-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Local host boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The standalone server shall listen only on localhost at an explicitly validated
port in 1024..65535, defaulting to 5087. It shall retain the 64 KiB request-body
bound and existing typed command validation, revision checks and structured
solver refusals. CLI configuration shall not enable public network binding.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-SCHEMATIC-SOLVER-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Explicit native solver availability
STATEMENT: >>>
The distribution may include an explicitly selected trusted solver with its
SHA-256 and source provenance, or accept an explicit absolute solver path.
A missing optional solver shall preserve schematic editing and the analytical
divider while native analyses return an explicit unavailable result. Missing
model providers or numerical outputs shall never be replaced with invented
successful results. Browser and MCP shall retain the shared command contracts.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-CSHARP-AUDIT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Evidence-based language modernization
STATEMENT: >>>
The migration shall document useful C# features adopted or already present and
their verified scope. Changes shall preserve public wire contracts and error,
cancellation and resource semantics. New syntax alone shall not establish a
performance improvement. Inapplicable or incompatible features shall be
documented rather than introduced solely for feature-count claims.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VELO-SCHEMATIC-VERIFICATION-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Reject partial test-framework success
STATEMENT: >>>
The schematic verification entry point shall validate the generated test report,
completed counts and required contract/property cases. A zero process exit or
nominally successful partial report shall not pass when an unhandled framework
exception, fatal error, aborted run or missing required case is present. Actual
executed counts, property replay and unavailable coverage shall remain explicit.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BOOK-BUNDLE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Executable standalone lesson package
STATEMENT: >>>
The standard standalone schematic package shall include its real simulation
executable, host runtime and browser assets. A representative RC lesson shall
execute from the extracted package outside a source checkout without a separate
solver installation. Optional provider/model dependencies and platform limits
shall be declared; a UI-only package shall not be described as a simulation bundle.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BOOK-LOCK-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Author-controlled layout lock
STATEMENT: >>>
A lesson author shall choose whether readers may unlock its layout. A locked
lesson shall preserve component identities, types, positions, orientations,
wiring, routes, named nets, junctions and hierarchy while permitting supported
parameter changes, inspection and simulation. The default general editor shall
remain editable and may expose a layout-lock checkbox.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BOOK-COMMAND-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Shared command enforcement and explicit refusals
STATEMENT: >>>
Layout policy shall be enforced by the shared typed command layer for browser,
keyboard, programmatic and MCP entry points. Refused operations shall return a
structured result, preserve state/history, and retain document/revision checks.
Disabling browser controls alone shall not implement this requirement.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BOOK-HISTORY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Persistence and undo preserve author policy
STATEMENT: >>>
Reader save/load, undo/redo and reset commands shall not relax a deployment's
author policy or bypass a layout lock. Parameter-only history may remain usable
while structural history is refused. Enabling a lock shall not erase author or
reader history. Old editable documents shall retain a documented default.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BOOK-LESSON-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Evidence-backed electronics lesson readiness
STATEMENT: >>>
The project shall maintain an electronics-topic, model and analysis readiness
matrix covering passive networks, diode circuits, bipolar and field-effect
transistor circuits, feedback amplifiers, filters, oscillators and switching.
Drawing availability shall remain separate from execution support and verified
lesson readiness. Each ready lesson shall include actual parameters, probes,
waveforms as applicable, expected results and independent reference evidence.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BOOK-EMBED-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Web and presentation embedding
STATEMENT: >>>
A lesson shall be embeddable in an HTML book or WALLY presentation with a
documented simulation-service dependency, author layout policy and independent
document identity. Offline packaging shall provide a usable local host path;
static HTML shall not be claimed to execute a native solver by itself.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SCH-BOOK-AGENT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Agent control of the visible embedded session
STATEMENT: >>>
An embedded automation integration shall address the same visible circuit and
document revision as the reader or presenter. It shall expose supported typed
commands, correlate outcomes, reject stale requests and validate message origins
and sources. A separate hidden MCP session shall not satisfy this requirement.
<<<
